From fc0a7a17ac80e65ea8bea86e69511f4becfa2af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:46:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add civ54 ruleset: a copy of civ45's one-unit-per-tile hex
 rules

civ45 is turning into a stacking game on a square map (Freeciv45). The
one-unit-per-tile rules of its first two slices (hex map, the Unit Move
and Transport Disembark limits, the Lua relocation with its
StacksAnywhere and StacksInPort exemptions, culture radius, cultural
victory, bombard range 2, strategic resources and three nation-unique
items) carry on unchanged as civ54, for the later game that needs
engine work. Registered in meson.build like civ45.
